,"sourceProvenanceId":"Ocran","sourceTitle":"Ocran"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Shelumiel","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":1,"href":"?bref=Num.2.12","rawReference":"Num.2.12"}],"ruleId":"Shelumiel::Shelumiel::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Shelumiel"},"text":"The tribe of Simeon will camp next to it. The leader of the Simeonites is Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai,","verse":12}],"id":"Shelumiel","label":"Shelumiel","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Shelumiel::Shelumiel::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Shelumiel","term":"Shelumiel"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Shelumiel","sourceTitle":"Shelumiel"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","phrase":"Tent of Meeting","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting"},"text":"“The Israelites are to camp around the Tent of Meeting at a distance from it, each man under his standard, with the banners of his family.","verse":2},{"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","phrase":"Tent of Meeting","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting"},"text":"In the middle of the camps, the Tent of Meeting is to travel with the camp of the Levites. They are to set out in the order they encamped, each in his own place under his standard.","verse":17}],"id":"Tabernacle","label":"Tent of Meeting","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","scope":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","senseReview":"The original publisher explicitly links this complete unambiguous name/phrase to this target. Redirect and target were reviewed once; actual BSB phrase and full word boundaries required. Target original title and complete article remain unchanged.","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting","term":"Tent of Meeting"}],"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","matchingRules":["source_verified_redirect"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Tabernacle","sourceTitle":"Tabernacle"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Zuar","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":1,"href":"?bref=Num.2.5","rawReference":"Num.2.5"}],"ruleId":"Zuar::Zuar::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Zuar"},"text":"The tribe of Issachar will camp next to it. The leader of the Issacharites is Nethanel son of Zuar,","verse":5}],"id":"Zuar","label":"Zuar","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Zuar::Zuar::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Zuar","term":"Zuar"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Zuar","sourceTitle":"Zuar"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Zurishaddai","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":1,"href":"?bref=Num.2.12","rawReference":"Num.2.12"}],"ruleId":"Zurishaddai::Zurishaddai::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Zurishaddai"},"text":"The tribe of Simeon will camp next to it. The leader of the Simeonites is Shelumiel son of Zurishaddai,","verse":12}],"id":"Zurishaddai","label":"Zurishaddai","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Zurishaddai::Zurishaddai::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Zurishaddai","term":"Zurishaddai"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Zurishaddai","sourceTitle":"Zurishaddai"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.2.1-34","r":"Num.2.1-34","rawR":"Num.2.1-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.1-34","value":"Num.2.1-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:1-34"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Israel’s camps were to be organized by tribal groupings. This arrangement may have reflected concerns for social status, access to water, and security for the Tabernacle, which represented the Lord’s presence. The Egyptian army from approximately this same era camped in a similar defensive formation to protect the sacred objects that accompanied their field campaigns."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.2.1-34","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":2,"endVerse":34,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.2.1-34","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"NUM","sourceChapterCoverage":[2],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"1f2c695dbb984b7a79ec2b2f6a666c6839587496d452e4c5a8acd003e386928d","sourceItemName":"Num.2.1-34","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1602,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"NUM","canonicalOSIS":"Num","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Num"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Num.2.1-34","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Num.2.1-34","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.2.2","r":"Num.2.2","rawR":"Num.2.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.2","value":"Num.2.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:2"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Each area of the Hebrew ",{"c":["camp"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," was identified by ",{"c":["family banners"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," which were probably flags or streamers (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.52","r":"Num.1.52","rawR":"Num.1.52","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.52","value":"Num.1.52"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:52"},"). The use of such tribal symbols or battle flags finds an analogy in modern bedouin life, where the divisions of tribe, clan, and family have long held great importance. • The tribes camped around the sanctuary at a safe distance (cp. ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.3.4","r":"Josh.3.4","rawR":"Josh.3.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.3.4","value":"Josh.3.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Josh 3:4"},") that respected the gap between God’s holiness and the non-Levitical tribes."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.2.2","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":2,"endVerse":2,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.2.2","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"NUM","sourceChapterCoverage":[2],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6db52169e94dd82ca4bebc24d6c7d116fe1d88bb4bd8089480803d80ebf51853","sourceItemName":"Num.2.2","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1603,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"NUM","canonicalOSIS":"Num","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Num"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Num.2.2","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Num.2.2","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.2.3-9","r":"Num.2.3-9","rawR":"Num.2.3-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.3-9","value":"Num.2.3-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:3-9"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The tribes of ",{"c":["Judah, Issachar, and Zebulun"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," camped in the most prestigious place ",{"c":["on the east side of the Tabernacle"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and led the way when Israel was on the move. This largest of the tribal groups (",{"c":["186,400"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},") could provide adequate protection for the sacred tent and its attendants."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.2.3-9","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":2,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.2.3-9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"NUM","sourceChapterCoverage":[2],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"35d2598b5753f9f4308d39fed1c5df7b34281612de1e905f32671661c0938bf2","sourceItemName":"Num.2.3-9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1604,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"NUM","canonicalOSIS":"Num","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Num"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Num.2.3-9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Num.2.3-9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.2.10-16","r":"Num.2.10-16","rawR":"Num.2.10-16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.10-16","value":"Num.2.10-16"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:10-16"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The tribes of ",{"c":["Reuben, Simeon, and Gad"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," camped ",{"c":["on the south"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". With their ",{"c":["151,450"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," warriors, they took second place in the line of march."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.2.10-16","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":2,"endVerse":16,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.2.10-16","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"NUM","sourceChapterCoverage":[2],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"4deda5f75ab6aa0746fd5e4376ff18de4a69a99487b775d35993b2cf54444c5d","sourceItemName":"Num.2.10-16","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":1605,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"NUM","canonicalOSIS":"Num","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"Num"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"Num.2.10-16","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"Num.2.10-16","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=Num.2.18-24","r":"Num.2.18-24","rawR":"Num.2.18-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.18-24","value":"Num.2.18-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:18-24"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The tribes of ",{"c":["Ephraim, Manasseh, and Benjamin"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," marched behind the Tabernacle and the Levites."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:Num.2.18-24","refs":[{"book":"NUM","endChapter":2,"endVerse":24,"startChapter":2,"startVerse":18}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Num.2.18-24","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename"